---
import ProjectLayout from "../../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro";
import ImageSlider from "../../../components/project/ImageSlider";
import SectionTitle from "../../../components/project/SectionTitle.astro";
import HighlightCard from "../../../components/project/HighlightCard.astro";

import cover from "../../../assets/kahosim/cover.png";
import cycle from "../../../assets/kahosim/cycle.png";
import applicantUi from "../../../assets/kahosim/applicant_ui.png";
import bankGuide from "../../../assets/kahosim/bank_guide.png";
import reviewerCanvas from "../../../assets/kahosim/reviewer_canvas.png";
import linebot from "../../../assets/kahosim/linebot.png";
---

<ProjectLayout
  title="Ka-Ho-Sim | Redesigning Youth Subsidy Applications at the Source"
  tags={["Meichu Hackathon 2nd Place", "GovTech", "Product Strategy", "On-Device OCR", "End-to-End Service Design"]}
>
  <div slot="aside" class="space-y-6">
    <ImageSlider
      images={[
        { src: cover.src, alt: "Ka-Ho-Sim project cover" },
        { src: cycle.src, alt: "The vicious rejection cycle in subsidy review" },
        { src: applicantUi.src, alt: "Redesigned applicant flow with dynamic fields" },
        { src: bankGuide.src, alt: "De-identified mobile banking tutorials" },
        { src: reviewerCanvas.src, alt: "Reviewer canvas with smart highlight extraction" },
        { src: linebot.src, alt: "Official LINE integration for status updates" },
      ]}
      client:load
    />
    <div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-2">
      <HighlightCard value="2nd Place" label="Meichu Hackathon (Maker Track)" />
      <HighlightCard value="72%" label="Existing Rejection Rate Uncovered" />
      <HighlightCard value="On-Device" label="Privacy OCR (PCI DSS v4.0)" />
    </div>
  </div>

  <SectionTitle title="Field Discovery: Beyond the Prompt" />
  <p>
    Built during the 2026 Meichu Hackathon (Maker Track), this project tackled Hsinchu City Government's "AI Youth Digital Tool Subsidy Program." To look beyond the written requirements, I reached out directly to the program's caseworker to understand the friction that the prompt never described.
  </p>
  <p>
    Three caseworkers managed the entire initiative, manually inspecting every submission. During peak periods, roughly 72 of every 100 daily applications were rejected for non-compliant documentation.
  </p>
  <p>
    More importantly, we uncovered the root cause: most applicants simply didn't know how to export eligible proof-of-payment statements from their specific mobile banking apps. People weren't being careless; the existing process simply never showed them what was required.
  </p>
  <p class="border-l-2 border-zinc-500 pl-4 text-zinc-300 italic">
    "That insight reshaped our strategy: review acceleration was critical, but speeding up internal workflows alone wouldn't solve the bottleneck if non-compliant files kept flooding in. We needed an end-to-end framework: guided application with on-device privacy OCR, canvas review with smart highlighting for caseworkers, and an intelligent LINE Bot bridge to eliminate phone gridlock."
  </p>

  <SectionTitle title="The Solution: A Three-Pillar Architecture" />

  <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-zinc-200 mt-4 mb-2">1. Applicant Web Flow: Guided Intake & On-Device Privacy OCR</h3>
  <ul class="list-disc ml-6 space-y-2">
    <li><strong class="text-zinc-200">Guided Step-by-Step Flow</strong>: Rebuilt the submission experience with clear document requirements and visual previews at every step, removing ambiguity before submission.</li>
    <li><strong class="text-zinc-200">On-Device Privacy & Redaction (PCI DSS v4.0)</strong>: Embedded client-side OCR using Tesseract.js with Luhn algorithm validation. Card numbers and personal data are masked locally in the browser before upload, so raw documents never leave the device. Designed against PCI DSS v4.0 Requirement 3.4.1.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-zinc-200 mt-6 mb-2">2. Caseworker Console: Canvas Review & Smart Highlighting</h3>
  <ul class="list-disc ml-6 space-y-2">
    <li><strong class="text-zinc-200">Canvas Review with Smart Highlighting</strong>: Unifies multi-page receipts on a single canvas and auto-highlights the details that matter for approval (subscription price, software name, applicant identity), so caseworkers no longer scan page by page.</li>
    <li><strong class="text-zinc-200">Self-Learning Software Whitelist</strong>: When an applicant applies for an unlisted AI tool, a caseworker verifies it once, and the system automatically updates the global eligible list for everyone going forward, eliminating duplicate research.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-zinc-200 mt-6 mb-2">3. Communication Bridge (LINE Bot): Banking Guides & Status Updates</h3>
  <ul class="list-disc ml-6 space-y-2">
    <li><strong class="text-zinc-200">Interactive Banking Guides</strong>: Built conversational, step-by-step walkthroughs showing applicants how to find and export monthly statements across major Taiwan banks (Cathay Cube, E.SUN Wallet, etc.), directly tackling the #1 cause of rejection.</li>
    <li><strong class="text-zinc-200">Proactive Notifications & Support Shield</strong>: Connected to the city's official youth account (@youthhsinchu) to push status updates and step-by-step resubmission guidance, reducing repetitive phone inquiries.</li>
  </ul>

  <SectionTitle title="My Role" />
  <ul class="list-disc ml-6 space-y-2">
    <li><strong class="text-zinc-200">Field Research & Problem Discovery</strong>: Initiated contact and interviewed the program caseworker, surfacing the quantified bottleneck: a 3-person team handling ~100 daily applications at a 72% rejection rate.</li>
    <li><strong class="text-zinc-200">Product Strategy & MVP Scoping</strong>: Established the three-pillar architecture (applicant intake + caseworker canvas + LINE Bot bridge) to maximize the 3-person team's capacity during the hackathon.</li>
    <li><strong class="text-zinc-200">Frontend & On-Device OCR Development</strong>: Built the applicant-facing web interface and implemented client-side OCR, card validation, and automatic data redaction using Tesseract.js.</li>
  </ul>

  <SectionTitle title="Why I Interviewed First This Time" />
  <p>
    This was my second hackathon. At the first one, a generative AI application hackathon, we skipped any preparation and started unpacking the brief on the day itself. Facing a large set of required modules with no shared understanding of the problem, we never converged, shipped only part of the scope, and did not place.
  </p>
  <p>
    So this time I contacted the caseworker and mapped the user journey before the event started. The difference was not building more; it was that the whole team could commit to one direction, because we had already decided which problem was worth solving.
  </p>

  <SectionTitle title="Outcome" />
  <p>
    Ka-Ho-Sim placed <strong>2nd in the Maker Track at the 2026 Meichu Hackathon</strong>, out of 12 teams.
  </p>
</ProjectLayout>
